    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d22-a5">

                <pb facs="0133" n="27" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg27"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5 in No.
                    184—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Kranz to Mr.
                            Grant</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Wicliczka</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-08-02"><hi rendition="#italic">August 2,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>It is not until to-day that my repeated requests made at the district captaincy
                    here for my son’s naturalization certificate have been granted, and I herewith
                    inclose it, in conformity with the contents of your note, in which you also
                    inform me of the intervention of the ministry of foreign affairs.</p>
                <pb facs="0134" n="28" xml:id="pg28"/>
                <p>The bail deposited by me has been returned to me. I would ask to have the
                    naturalization certificate returned to me after you have examined it.</p>
                <p>After having recovered his health my son intends to stay here two weeks and then
                    return home to New Orleans.</p>
                <p>Rendering to you my sincerest thanks for the prompt and kind protection offered,
                    and assuring you of my highest respect,</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Salomon Kranz</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
